    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but that's just another way of romanticizing a void. \"experimenting\" or \"finding new patterns\" requires a drive that I just don't have anymore. the more I look at the math and the biology, the more it feels like a closed loop. there's no \"deeper connection\" to find, because there's nothing there to connect to. it's just a void. it feels like the only honest response to realizing that everything is hollow is to just... stop trying to fill it.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
